        "original_id": "35f2a811-6d26-5720-9b75-263c85f028d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Noonan, Neal Scanlan\n- Films: Babe, Miss Potter\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Director, Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay, Academy Award for Best Visual Effects\n- Organizations: Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences\n\nFacts:\n- Chris Noonan was born on 14 November 1952 and is a Sydney-based Australian filmmaker and actor.\n- The Academy Award for Best Director, officially called the Academy Award for Best Directing, is presented annually by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.\n- In 1995, Chris Noonan was best known for the family film Babe.\n- Chris Noonan was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director and the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay for Babe.\n- In 1996, Neal Scanlan won the Academy Award for Best Visual Effects for the film Babe.\n- In 2006, Chris Noonan directed Miss Potter, an Anglo-American biographical fiction family drama film.",
